                <pb facs="0688" n="600" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg600"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Foster to Mr.
                            Newberry.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-10-14"><hi rendition="#italic">October 14,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 402.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 547 of the 26th
                    ultimo. It concerns the seizure of Bibles at Geybizé, a town within the limits
                    of the vilayet of Constantinople and your efforts with the grand vizier to
                    effect their release.</p>
                <p>The Department patiently awaits the result of that officer’s telegram directing
                    the return of the Bibles and ordering future noninterference in such case.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John W. Foster.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
